			<div class="content" id="post-content-1916975">
									

<p>I used to have a lot of cracked computer games when I was a kid, so I found that pretty amusing (it was not uncommon to keep a shitty game just because it had a great crack intro). But overall it felt a bit simplistic and didn't take the idea very far. It seems rather pointless to have obviously counterfeit pieces of art when you can get reproductions anywhere. I think this idea could be more effectively used for something else, but I don't have suggestions right now. Neutral vote for me.</p>
